🚀 Excited to share my latest project: PolicyAI — an AI-Powered Economic Policy Intelligence Platform

I recently developed PolicyAI, a full-stack platform designed to transform economic data into interactive policy simulations, forecasts, comparisons, and actionable intelligence.

Instead of building a static dashboard, the goal was to create a real, backend-integrated decision-support system where visualizations and analytical results are driven by actual API responses rather than dummy data.

🔹 What PolicyAI includes

🌍 Economic Data Explorer — Explore historical country-level economic indicators using World Bank data.

📊 Policy Simulation — Configure economic scenarios by adjusting variables such as investment, FDI, exports, imports, government consumption, and household consumption.

📈 Forecasting & Visualization — Generate multi-year projections using forecasting models and visualize baseline vs. scenario trajectories.

⚖️ Scenario Comparison — Compare persisted simulation runs through interactive cards and projection graphs.

🧠 Economic Intelligence — Analyze regional and sector-level economic information through interactive visualizations.

🤖 AI Policy Assistant — Natural-language interaction powered through a local Ollama/LLM integration.

📄 Policy Reports — Generate reports from actual saved scenario results.

🌗 Complete Dark & Light Experience — A responsive futuristic interface with consistent theme adaptation across the entire application.

🛠️ Technology Stack

Frontend: React, Vite, JavaScript, CSS
Backend: FastAPI, Python, SQLAlchemy
Data: World Bank API
ML: Autoregressive forecasting & XGBoost
AI: Ollama + Qwen
Database: SQLite / PostgreSQL support
API Architecture: REST-based frontend/backend integration

One principle I maintained throughout development was:

If the backend does not provide the data, the frontend does not invent it.

Missing information is handled through proper loading, empty, and error states rather than fabricated numbers.

PolicyAI demonstrates how AI, machine learning, economic data, interactive visualization, and modern full-stack development can come together in a single decision-support platform.

Looking forward to continuing to improve its forecasting, intelligence, and policy-analysis capabilities.

